  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Merlin is advancing its autonomous flight technology toward certification, having achieved the first fully automated takeoffs on certification candidate aircraft in both the U.S. and New Zealand. The launch of its first product, Condor, targets multi-crew large aircraft for civil applications, signaling a move from development toward commercial readiness. End-market interest appears supportive, though the company remains pre-revenue, and regulatory milestones are still ahead.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership strengthened the balance sheet through an $80 million PIPE from an existing fundamental institutional shareholder, extending the cash runway and demonstrating insider confidence. The team is deploying this capital to accelerate program execution and hit key 2026–2027 milestones, while completing the business combination that brought MRLN to the public markets. Execution is focused on transitioning from technology demonstration to certification and commercial launch, a path that now appears better funded and schedule-driven.",
